+                + fnp.outer(sigma, mu_pre) * pdf_i * cond_ji
+                + sigma_outer * one_minus_r2 * joint_pdf
+            )
+            cov = second - fnp.outer(mu, mu)
+            cov = cov - fnp.diag(fnp.diagonal(cov)) + fnp.diag(var)
+            cov = 0.5 * (cov + cov.T)
             rows.append(mu)
+
         return fnp.stack(rows, axis=0)

codex
The evaluation remains active past three minutes. That is still compatible with 50 independent subprocess evaluations, but it makes a leaner covariance update attractive even if accuracy improves. I’ll use this result as the accuracy ceiling, then test a first-order covariance transport that removes all pairwise CDF quadrature.
