+            cov = 0.5 * (cov + cov.T)
             rows.append(mu)
+
         return fnp.stack(rows, axis=0)

codex
The first hybrid improves again, to `2.7680e-06` (31.4× baseline). I’m now attacking probe variance directly: eight randomized orthonormal direction bases replace independent directions, so each block integrates every spherical quadratic exactly. I’m also upgrading the fast covariance closure with Hermite terms through order four; this approximates the exact bivariate Gaussian covariance at negligible cost.
